## Code Style Rules

### TypeScript/React

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
import type { FileBlame } from '@angkorgit/core';  // Type imports first
import { useUi } from '@/features/ui/store';

// Interactive elements need full accessibility
<div
  role="button"
  tabIndex={0}
  aria-label="Clear filters"
  onClick={handleClick}
  onKeyDown={(e) => {
    if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ') {
      e.preventDefault();
      handleClick();
    }
  }}
>

// Colors via tokens only
className="bg-surface text-foreground"  // ✅
style={{ color: '#d97706' }}            // ❌ Never hex in components
```

### Rust

```rust
// Commands stay thin
#[tauri::command]
#[allow(non_snake_case)]
pub async fn file_blame(file: String, rev: Option<String>) -> Result<FileBlame, AppError> {
    blocking(move || core::blame::blame_file(&file, rev.as_deref())).await
}

// Everything blocking goes through spawn_blocking
// Operations that can pause return OpOutcome, not errors for conflicts
```

## Testing Requirements

### Test Pyramid (from Testing-Guide.md)

```
         /\
        /  \      E2E: 13 tests (~43s)
       /____\     Use for: Critical user flows only
      /      \    
     / Unit   \   Unit: 158 tests (<1s)
    /  Tests   \  Use for: Logic, structure, accessibility
   /____________\ 
```

**Rule**: 能下沉的下沉 (Push tests down the pyramid)

### What to Test Where

**Unit Tests** (`tests/unit/*.test.ts`):
- Pure functions and data transformations
- Accessibility attributes (role, tabIndex, aria-*)
- Component structure (no duplicate menu items)
- Edge cases (empty, single, max, missing data)

**E2E Tests** (`tests/e2e/smoke.test.ts`):
- Critical user journeys only
- Use semantic selectors: `getByRole('button')` not `.css-class`
- Helper functions for common actions
- Screenshots on failure

**Rust Tests** (`apps/desktop/src-tauri/tests/git_engine.rs`):
- Every new engine function
- Real git repos in temp dirs
- Integration with libgit2

### Demo Mode

All IPC commands support demo mode:
```typescript
// ipc.ts
export async function fileBlame(file: string, rev: string | null): Promise<FileBlame> {
  if (isDemoMode()) {
    return demoFileBlame(file, rev);  // Synthetic data
  }
  return invoke('file_blame', { file, rev });
}
```

## Quality Checklist (from Quality-Checklist.md)

### Before Starting (Design Phase)

- [ ] Interactive elements need `role`, `tabIndex`, `aria-label`, `onKeyDown`
- [ ] Grep codebase to avoid duplicating existing logic
- [ ] Plan unit tests first (TDD approach)

### Before Committing

- [ ] Run `bun run format:check && bun run typecheck && bun test`
- [ ] Run `cargo fmt --check && cargo clippy && cargo test` (if Rust changed)
- [ ] Pre-commit hook auto-formats and organizes imports
- [ ] Unit tests cover new logic, E2E tests cover critical flows

### Before PR

- [ ] All local CI checks pass (see Quality-Checklist.md § 4)
- [ ] Documentation updated (CHANGELOG, CLAUDE.md if architecture changed)
- [ ] Test counts in PR match actual test files
- [ ] Screenshots attached (for UI changes, both themes)

## Common Patterns

### Adding a New Feature

1. **Check CLAUDE.md § 8 (Gotchas)** — Has this been tried before?
2. **Design with accessibility** — role/aria/keyboard from day 1
3. **Write unit tests first** — Fast feedback, precise errors
4. **Implement in small commits** — One logical change per commit
5. **Add E2E test if critical path** — User flow, not implementation
6. **Update docs** — CHANGELOG + CLAUDE.md if architectural

### Fixing a Bug

1. **Check CLAUDE.md § 8** — Is this a known gotcha?
2. **Write failing test** — Unit test preferred over E2E
3. **Fix the bug** — Minimal change
4. **Verify test passes** — Run full test suite
5. **Add to Quality-Checklist.md** — If it's a recurring pattern

### Debugging E2E Failures

**Wrong approach** ❌:
- Increase timeout
- Add random waits
- Retry logic

**Right approach** ✅:
1. Take screenshot: `await page.screenshot({ path: 'debug.png' })`
2. Check element exists: `await page.pause()` (opens inspector)
3. Verify attributes: Missing `role="button"`? Add it
4. Root cause > symptom: Fix missing attribute, not timeout

## File Organization

```
apps/desktop/
├── src/                       # React frontend (see CLAUDE.md § 6)
│   ├── core/
│   │   ├── ipc.ts            # THE typed IPC boundary
│   │   └── demo.ts           # Demo mode synthetic data
│   ├── features/             # Feature-based organization
│   └── components/           # Shared components
└── src-tauri/                # Rust backend (see CLAUDE.md § 5)
    ├── src/
    │   ├── commands.rs       # Thin Tauri command layer
    │   └── core/             # Git engine (one module per domain)
    └── tests/
        └── git_engine.rs     # Integration tests (73 tests)

packages/
├── core/                     # Pure TypeScript domain logic
└── design-system/            # UI primitives

tests/
├── unit/                     # Vitest (158 tests, <1s)
└── e2e/                      # Playwright (13 tests, ~43s)

docs/
├── README.md                 # Documentation hub (START HERE)
├── Quality-Checklist.md      # Quality gates
├── Testing-Guide.md          # Test strategies
└── ...
```

## Import Aliases

```typescript
@/                           → apps/desktop/src
@angkorgit/core              → packages/core/src
@angkorgit/design-system     → packages/design-system/src
```

## Pre-commit Hook

Located at `.git/hooks/pre-commit`:
- Runs `biome check --write --organize-imports-enabled=true`
- Auto-formats code and organizes imports
- Must match CI checks exactly

If pre-commit passes but CI fails → hook is broken, needs update.

## CI Workflow

Triggered by:
- Push to `main`
- PR with `ci` label
- Manual dispatch

Stages:
1. Format check (`biome ci .`)
2. Typecheck (all packages)
3. Unit tests
4. Build
5. E2E tests (if changed)
6. Rust lint + tests (3 platforms)

**Optimization**: Uses path filters, fail-fast, parallel matrix builds

## Forbidden Patterns

❌ **Never do**:
- Hex colors in components (use tokens only)
- `console.log` in production code
- `any` type without justification
- Interactive `<div>` without `role`/`aria`/`onKeyDown`
- E2E tests for non-critical paths (use unit tests)
- Pre-commit hook out of sync with CI
- Duplicate menu items (consolidate into shared components)

## When in Doubt

1. Search [CLAUDE.md](./CLAUDE.md) for similar patterns
2. Check [docs/Quality-Checklist.md](./docs/Quality-Checklist.md) for process
3. Grep codebase for existing implementations
4. Ask in team chat with context

## Useful Commands

```bash
# Development
bun run dev                  # Browser demo mode
bun tauri:dev                # Full app with hot reload

# Testing
bun test                     # Unit tests
bun test --watch             # Watch mode
bun run test:e2e             # E2E tests
cd apps/desktop/src-tauri && cargo test  # Rust tests

# Quality Checks
bun run format:check         # Biome format + imports
bun run typecheck            # All packages
bun run build                # Production build

# Pre-PR (run all)
bun run format:check && bun run typecheck && bun test && bun run test:e2e
```

